#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Systemsettings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "locale"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "country"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "language"
msgstr "lenga"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This module of the &kde; &systemsettings; allows you select customization "
"options that depend on the region of the world that you happen to live in. "
"There are five different tabs in this module, each of which is described in "
"detail in the following sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In most cases, you can simply select the country and the language, and the "
"other options will be set in an appropriate manner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the tabs of this module, you can see a preview of what the settings "
"look like. In addition to positive and negative numbers, you can see how "
"positive and negative currency values, long and short dates, and times are "
"displayed. When you change any of the settings, the preview shows the "
"effects of the changes before you apply them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "Locale"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the top of the this tab you can select the country or region that you "
"want to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you click on <guilabel>change</guilabel>, a dialog pops up showing "
"major groups of countries. You can select one of these regions and see a "
"list of the countries that are available for that region."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The settings for numbers, money, date and time will automatically switch to "
"the corresponding values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main part of this tab is a list of all available languages. The &GUI; of "
"&kde; programs will be displayed in the first language in this list. If the "
"first language in the list is not available, the second will be used, &etc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the buttons on the left side of the list you can move the order of a "
"highlighted language up and down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guilabel>Add Language</guilabel> drop down box to add a "
"language to the list. If the language is already in the list, it will be "
"moved up to the first place in the list instead."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "If only US English is available, no translations have been installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that some applications and documentations may not be translated to your "
"language; in this case, they will automatically fall back to US English."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Language and Country/Region are independent settings. Changing a language "
"does <emphasis>not</emphasis> automatically change the settings for numbers, "
"currency &etc; to the corresponding country or region."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Numbers"
msgstr "Nombres"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this page, you can select options for how numbers are displayed. The "
"defaults are selected automatically based on the country which is currently "
"selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the text box labeled <guilabel>Decimal symbol</guilabel>, you can type "
"the character that you want to use to separate the decimal portion of "
"numbers. You could put anything here you wanted to, but really, <userinput>."
"</userinput> and <userinput>,</userinput> are the two characters that make "
"the most sense."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similarly, you can choose the character which is used to group units of "
"thousands in numbers. If no character, not even a space, is present, then "
"there will be no separator for thousands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following two text boxes allow you to choose what character should be "
"prefixed to positive and negative numbers respectively. For example, the "
"default for English is not to have any prefix for positive numbers, and a "
"<userinput>-</userinput> for negative numbers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the spinbox <guilabel>Dezimal places</guilabel> you can set the number of "
"decimal places displayed for numeric values, &ie;. the number of digits "
"<emphasis>after</emphasis> the decimal separator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Digit set</guilabel> drop down box presents digit sets which "
"may be used instead of basic Arabic when displaying numbers. If you select a "
"digit set other than Arabic, it will be applied only to numbers which appear "
"in language context that admits this set (e.g. Arabic-Indic digits in "
"application translated to Arabic language), while Arabic digits are still "
"going to be used elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that decimal symbol, thousands separator, decimal places and the set of "
"digits used to display monetary values has to be set separately on the "
"<guilabel>Money</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Money"
msgstr "Argent"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unlike the display of ordinary numbers, conventions for currency values do "
"vary from region to region. However, you will find that the defaults are "
"probably fine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The character or characters representing the currency symbol are based on "
"the country that is currently selected. The decimal symbol, thousands "
"separator, decimal places, and digit set for money work as they do for "
"numbers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For both positive and negative currency values, you can control whether the "
"currency symbol appears before or after the numeric value, and how the sign "
"of the value is distinguished in the display. Note that the symbols used for "
"the sign of currency values are the same as those used for other numeric "
"values."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the check box labeled <guilabel>Prefix currency symbol</guilabel> is "
"selected, the currency symbol appears before the numeric value. If this "
"check box is cleared, then the currency symbol appears after the numeric "
"value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are five choices for the way in which the sign of the currency value "
"is handled:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Parentheses around</guilabel> option displays the numeric "
"value within a pair of parentheses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Before Quantity Money</guilabel> option displays the sign "
"before the numeric value, but after any currency symbol that may be present."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>After Quantity Money</guilabel> option displays the sign after "
"the numeric value, but before any currency symbol that may be present."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Before Money</guilabel> option displays the sign before the "
"numeric value as well as any currency symbol that may be present."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>After Money</guilabel> option displays the sign after the "
"numeric value as well as any currency symbol that may be present."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid "Time &amp; Dates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use a different calendar system than Gregorian, you can choose this "
"from the first drop down box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next option determines if the Common Era (CE/BCE) should be used instead "
"of the Christian Era (AD/BC)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Likewise, if numbers in date and time strings should use digits other than "
"basic Arabic, another set of digits can be selected from the second drop "
"down box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the rest of this page, there are text boxes for the time, long date, and "
"short date, in which you can type format strings to control the way in which "
"times and dates are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Except for the special codes described below, any other characters in the "
"format strings are displayed literally. The special codes consist of a "
"<parameter>%</parameter> sign followed by a character, as shown in the list "
"of codes below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "Time format codes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>HH</parameter> - The hour according to a 24-hour clock, using two "
"digits (00 to 23)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>hH</parameter> - The hour according to a 24-hour clock, using one "
"or two digits (0 to 23)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>PH</parameter> (uppercase <quote>p</quote>) - The hour according "
"to a 12-hour clock, using two digits (01 to 12)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>pH</parameter> (lowercase <quote>p</quote>) - The hour according "
"to a 12-hour clock, using one or two digits (1 to 12)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>MM</parameter> - The current minute using two digits (00 to 59)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>SS</parameter> - The current second using two digits (00 to 59)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>AMPM</parameter> - Either <quote>am</quote> or <quote>pm</quote> "
"depending on the hour. Useful with <parameter>PH</parameter> or "
"<parameter>pH</parameter>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date format codes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>YYYY</parameter> - The year, using 4 digits."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>YY</parameter> - The year, using 2 digits."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>MM</parameter> - The month, using 2 digits (01 to 12)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>mM</parameter> - The month, using 1 or 2 digits (1 to 12)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>MONTH</parameter> - The name of the month."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>SHORTMONTH</parameter> - The abbreviated name of the month."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>DD</parameter> - The day, using 2 digits (01 to 31)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>dD</parameter> - The day, using 1 or 2 digits (1 to 31)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>WEEKDAY</parameter> - The name of the weekday."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<parameter>SHORTWEEKDAY</parameter> - The abbreviated name of the weekday."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, there are four combo boxes which let you select the first day, the "
"first and last working day of the week and the day of the week for religious "
"observance in your country."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other"
msgstr "Autre"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select the default paper format with the combo box labeled "
"<guilabel>Paper Format</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the drop down box labeled <guilabel>Measure system</guilabel> to select "
"Imperial or Metric systems of measurement."
msgstr ""
